  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145628",
      "title": "Introducing Static Generation with \"getStaticProps\"",
      "lectureOrder": 266,
      "videoOrder": 247,
      "sourceHash": "df1315701456ad2aaafde34e56eb8a73d4d7575278395ba8877f25be8836d923",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.17,
          "end": 3.08,
          "en": "So, let's explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.08,
          "end": 5.86,
          "en": "this first form of pre-rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.86,
          "end": 9.55,
          "en": "or of data fetching with Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.55,
          "end": 12.68,
          "en": "And that would be the Static Generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.68,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "which I did mention is typically recommended,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 18.68,
          "en": "but of course, I will explain all the details now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.68,
          "end": 21.16,
          "en": "and throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.16,
          "end": 23.09,
          "en": "Now, with Static Generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.09,
          "end": 24.63,
          "en": "there is a simple idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.63,
          "end": 29.48,
          "en": "The idea is that you pre-generate a page during build time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.48,
          "end": 33,
          "en": "And pre-generate means that all the HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33,
          "end": 35.62,
          "en": "and all the data that makes up the content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.62,
          "end": 38.09,
          "en": "is prepared in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.09,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "So, on the server side though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 42.11,
          "en": "that can be confusing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.11,
          "end": 43.83,
          "en": "With that I really mean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 45.88,
          "en": "during the build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.88,
          "end": 48.97,
          "en": "where you are allowed to execute code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.97,
          "end": 52.15,
          "en": "that would normally only run on the server side, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.15,
          "end": 55.68,
          "en": "Code that interacts with the file system, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.68,
          "end": 58.64,
          "en": "And you're going to see it in action very soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.64,
          "end": 61.96,
          "en": "So, data and pages are prepared during build time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.96,
          "end": 65.86,
          "en": "when you build your application before you deploy it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.86,
          "end": 70.33,
          "en": "Now, because pages are then pre-built during build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.33,
          "end": 72.23,
          "en": "once you deploy them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.23,
          "end": 75.25,
          "en": "they can be cached by the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.25,
          "end": 78.19,
          "en": "by the CDN that might be serving your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.19,
          "end": 80.64,
          "en": "And therefore, incoming requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 85.64,
          "en": "can be served instantly with those pre-built pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.82,
          "end": 88.06,
          "en": "Now, then, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.06,
          "end": 90.68,
          "en": "those pages after they were served,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.68,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "are still hydrated with your React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 97.36,
          "en": "So, you still have a regular React app in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.36,
          "end": 99.47,
          "en": "The only difference is that the pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.47,
          "end": 101.32,
          "en": "which are sent to your clients,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.32,
          "end": 103.13,
          "en": "are not empty initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.13,
          "end": 105.59,
          "en": "but pre populated with content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.59,
          "end": 108.35,
          "en": "Thereafter, you can still do whatever you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.35,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "It's still a regular React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 114.88,
          "en": "So, therefore, now, one main question, of course is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.88,
          "end": 117.34,
          "en": "how do we tell Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.34,
          "end": 120.68,
          "en": "that a certain page should be pre-generated?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.68,
          "end": 122.96,
          "en": "And how do we tell Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.96,
          "end": 126.85,
          "en": "which data is needed to pre-generate a page?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.85,
          "end": 128.3,
          "en": "And the answer is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.3,
          "end": 130.45,
          "en": "there is a specific function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.45,
          "end": 135.22,
          "en": "which we can export from inside our page components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.22,
          "end": 139.62,
          "en": "And that's important only from inside our page components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 142.16,
          "en": "not from our React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.16,
          "end": 144.96,
          "en": "but only from inside the component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.96,
          "end": 147.1,
          "en": "that live in our pages folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.1,
          "end": 148.18,
          "en": "From in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.18,
          "end": 153.097,
          "en": "we can export the special async function, getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.64,
          "end": 156.86,
          "en": "Now, that name matters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.86,
          "end": 160.9,
          "en": "It must be written exactly like this, getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.9,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "because that is then a function Next.js will watch out for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 168.43,
          "en": "Its async, which means it returns a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.43,
          "end": 170.82999999999998,
          "en": "and you can use the await keyword in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.82999999999998,
          "end": 175.02,
          "en": "And then, the special thing is that in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.02,
          "end": 176.78,
          "en": "you can run any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.78,
          "end": 180.38,
          "en": "that would normally run on the server side only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.38,
          "end": 181.46,
          "en": "So, in that function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.46,
          "end": 183.7,
          "en": "you don't run the client side code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.7,
          "end": 186.14,
          "en": "you're not restricted to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.14,
          "end": 190.17,
          "en": "and you don't have access to certain client side API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 190.17,
          "end": 193.86,
          "en": "you don't have access to the window object, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.86,
          "end": 196.57999999999998,
          "en": "but instead, you can run any code you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.57999999999998,
          "end": 200.03,
          "en": "that normally would only run on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.03,
          "end": 201.65,
          "en": "And even better than that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.65,
          "end": 205.93,
          "en": "code that you write inside of this getStaticProps function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.93,
          "end": 209.03,
          "en": "will not be included in the code bundle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.03,
          "end": 211.62,
          "en": "that's sent back to your clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.62,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "So, any code you put in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 216.35,
          "en": "will never be seen by your clients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.35,
          "end": 218.98,
          "en": "So, if you for example have code in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.98,
          "end": 221.8,
          "en": "that contains database credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.8,
          "end": 224.92000000000002,
          "en": "you typically wouldn't want to expose those credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.92000000000002,
          "end": 226.32,
          "en": "on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.32,
          "end": 229.74,
          "en": "You can safely write it inside of getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 233.99,
          "en": "because that code will never end up on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.99,
          "end": 236.8,
          "en": "And therefore, let's now take a closer look at that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.8,
          "end": 238.91,
          "en": "and let's start writing some code there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.91,
          "end": 242.573,
          "en": "so that we fully understand this function and how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
